From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Davis <1709934+Savid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:36:46 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ai): auth gateway logs why a conversation's message
 thread starts over

A message-thread create uploads the whole conversation, and the cache
entries its thread's continues wrote are not read by it: on a long agent
conversation one create writes hundreds of thousands of tokens to the cache.
Through the auth gateway, an Amp thread of about 470k tokens wrote close to
500k tokens to the cache every one to two minutes for an hour, and nothing in
the log said why its thread kept starting over.

The gateway's request line now carries the request's session id, how it
found its retained state (`client-key`, `history` with the messages appended
since, or `new`), how many sessions it retains, and Amp's thread id when Amp
sends one. The Anthropic provider logs each turn's thread decision at debug:
a continue with what it appends; a create with its reason (no anchor, replay,
expired, changed fields, or the message the history diverged at); or no
thread, and why. It also logs why a finished turn was not stored as
continuable, and the dropped-thinking lines carry the session id.

Logging only: requests are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
